{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2181","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2181","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2181\",\"parent_revision\":\"71eb39902259e07d50c238feea76d3b7733148db9e612cc56107d2d2c15a01ce\",\"root_revision\":\"71eb39902259e07d50c238feea76d3b7733148db9e612cc56107d2d2c15a01ce\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED**\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Create a `dh:multi-perspective-review` skill that dispatches four independent perspective reviewer agents (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility) in parallel against a diff, collects structured verdicts, and gates the pipeline on all-APPROVE.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` exists and is invocable\\n- Four agent `.md` files at `plugins/development-harness/agents/reviewer-{security,performance,quality,accessibility}.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lists `dh:multi-perspective-review` in its quality gate section\\n- A reference file `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/references/verdict-schema.md` defining the verdict block and SKIP detection rules\\n\\nScope boundaries:\\n- In-scope: skill file, 4 agent files, verdict-schema reference, complete-implementation update\\n- Out-of-scope: #1430 confidence gating / deduplication pipeline\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n\\n1. Agent file format | Requires: confirmed `.md` agent format and frontmatter conventions | Why: agents must be discoverable by `agent_profile/discovery.py`\\n2. Dispatch mechanism | Requires: confirmed `TeamCreate` + `dh:task-worker` pattern | Why: skill dispatches 4 parallel workers\\n3. profile_load routing | Requires: confirmed how `task-worker` receives perspective agent name | Why: each worker must specialize per perspective\\n4. Verdict schema | Requires: defined structure `{perspective, verdict, findings}` and SKIP detection rule | Why: orchestrator must parse all four verdicts uniformly\\n5. SKIP detection rule | Requires: file pattern that determines \\\"no UI changes\\\" | Why: Accessibility reviewer must emit SKIP without blocking when no UI files changed\\n6. Consolidation without #1430 | Requires: stub logic for pre-#1430 state | Why: #1430 is in-progress; skill must ship a working v1 now\\n7. complete-implementation integration | Requires: knowing where/how to insert `dh:multi-perspective-review` into quality gate list | Why: AC#7 requires this update\\n8. Existing skill/agent reference patterns | Requires: `code-reviewer.md` and `forensic-review/SKILL.md` as templates | Why: perspective agents follow same pattern\\n9. Non-zero exit on REJECT | Requires: skill must exit non-zero when any perspective rejects | Why: gates the pipeline\\n\\nVerification:\\n\\n- Agent file format: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/agent_profile/discovery.py` lines 7, 203-256 confirm `.md` files only; `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` is the reference template\\n- Dispatch mechanism: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 84-94 document `TeamCreate(\\\"impl-{slug}\\\")` + `dh:task-worker` as the standard parallel dispatch pattern\\n- profile_load routing: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `implement-feature/SKILL.md` line 98 + `development-harness/references/role-resolution-protocol.md` lines 102: `task-worker` reads `agent:` field from SAM task YAML via `sam_task` \u2192 calls `profile_load(agent_name=...)` internally; orchestrator dispatches only `dh:task-worker`\\n- Verdict schema: DERIVABLE | Basis: item defines `{perspective, verdict: APPROVE|REJECT|SKIP, findings: [...]}` with summary format `Security: APPROVE (0 findings) | ...`; schema must be formalized in `verdict-schema.md`\\n- SKIP detection rule: DERIVABLE | Basis: item text states \\\"no UI changes\\\" triggers SKIP for Accessibility; detection rule (file extensions / path patterns) must be defined in `verdict-schema.md` \u2014 reasonable default: any changed file matching `*.html`, `*.css`, `*.tsx`, `*.jsx`, UI component patterns\\n- Consolidation without #1430: AVAILABLE | Evidence: item explicitly states \\\"stub fallback \u2014 collect four verdicts, apply all-APPROVE gate\\\"; #1430 consolidation is additive when it lands\\n- complete-implementation integration: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` line 449 shows T1 Code Review as an existing quality gate; `dh:multi-perspective-review` is listed alongside `dh:forensic-review`\\n- Existing skill/agent reference patterns: AVAILABLE | Evidence: `code-reviewer.md` provides frontmatter template; `forensic-review/SKILL.md` provides single-pass predecessor\\n- Non-zero exit on REJECT: AVAILABLE | Evidence: item explicitly states \\\"exits non-zero when any perspective rejects\\\" in both Expected Behavior and Measurable Signal sections\\n\\nDecision:\\n- **APPROVED**\\n\\nAssumptions to Confirm (DERIVABLE only):\\n- Verdict schema structure | Basis: item text + AC#3/#6 | Validation step: define in `verdict-schema.md` at implementation start; review with item author if summary format needs adjustment\\n- SKIP detection rule (file patterns) | Basis: \\\"no UI changes\\\" from item text | Validation step: define pattern list in `verdict-schema.md`; default `*.html|*.css|*.tsx|*.jsx|*.vue|**/components/**` is a safe starting point \u2014 implementor may expand\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **multi-perspective parallel review skill (security/performance/quality/accessibility) over the same diff** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 pattern: 4-perspective code review (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility) via reviewer agent in /harness-review\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Closes the gap between single-pass forensic review and multi-angle coverage. Security and performance blind spots in the current single-agent pass are high-risk. Complementary to #1430 (in-progress) which cannot produce output without per-perspective inputs.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: #1430 (confidence gating/deduplication pipeline) cannot operate without per-perspective structured inputs \u2014 this item is #1430's upstream dependency.\\n- Bottleneck: Current `dh:forensic-review` runs one agent per task; security, performance, and accessibility concerns are surfaced only if the single reviewer happens to notice them.\\n- Affects: Every use of `dh:forensic-review` / `dh:complete-implementation` quality gate that touches code with security-relevant patterns.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Security, performance, quality, and accessibility concerns are caught in parallel in a single review wave, not missed when a generalist reviewer deprioritises them.\\n- Provides structured verdict inputs (#1430 can consume) \u2014 unblocks the deduplication/confidence pipeline.\\n- Follows the validated pattern from Claude Code Harness v4 (Reviewer agent with 4 perspectives per diff, effort level `xhigh`) \u2014 see `research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md`.\\n- SKIP verdict for accessibility when no UI changes avoids wasted agent spawns.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen invoked after a diff is available, the skill spawns four reviewer agents in parallel. Each agent examines the same changed files through a single perspective lens and returns a structured verdict block containing perspective name, APPROVE/REJECT/SKIP verdict, and a findings list. The skill collects all four verdicts and prints a one-line summary per perspective. If any perspective returns REJECT, the skill exits non-zero and surfaces the blocking findings. SKIP is a passing outcome and does not block the pipeline.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill orchestrating four parallel reviewer dispatches via `TeamCreate`.\\n- Four new agent definition files under `plugins/development-harness/agents/`: `reviewer-security.md`, `reviewer-performance.md`, `reviewer-quality.md`, `reviewer-accessibility.md`. Each agent file follows the existing `.md` format (not YAML) consistent with how `profile_load` discovers agents via `agent_profile/discovery.py`.\\n- A reference file `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/references/verdict-schema.md` defining the structured verdict block and SKIP detection rules.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` updated to list `dh:multi-perspective-review` as an available quality gate alongside forensic-review.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` exists with a `TeamCreate` dispatch loop spawning four `dh:task-worker` agents.\\n2. Four agent definition `.md` files exist at `plugins/development-harness/agents/reviewer-{security,performance,quality,accessibility}.md`, each with `user-invocable: false` and a perspective-scoped instruction body.\\n3. Each reviewer agent returns a structured verdict block: `{perspective, verdict: APPROVE|REJECT|SKIP, findings: [...]}`.\\n4. Running the skill against a diff with a known security issue (e.g., a hardcoded secret) produces `Security: REJECT (1 finding)` and exits non-zero.\\n5. Running the skill against a diff that touches no UI code produces `Accessibility: SKIP (no UI changes)` and does not block the pipeline.\\n6. The summary output format matches: `Security: APPROVE (0 findings) | Performance: REJECT (1 finding) | Quality: APPROVE (2 minor) | Accessibility: SKIP (no UI changes)`.\\n7. `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` references `dh:multi-perspective-review` in its quality gate list.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:forensic-review \u2014 predecessor single-pass review (157 lines, `dh:code-reviewer` dispatch) |\\n| Skill | /dh:code-review-python, /dh:code-review-typescript, /dh:code-review-cli, /dh:code-review-web, /dh:code-review-nodejs, /dh:code-review-llm, /dh:code-review-claude-skills \u2014 existing per-stack reviewers loaded by code-reviewer agent |\\n| Agent | @dh:code-reviewer \u2014 existing single-pass reviewer agent; perspective agents will follow same pattern |\\n| Agent | @dh:task-worker \u2014 required dispatch agent per dh CLAUDE.md extension rule |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/agent_profile/server.py \u2014 `profile_load` tool; discovers `.md` agent files only |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/agent_profile/discovery.py \u2014 agent file discovery mechanism |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md \u2014 reference agent file structure |\\n| Prior work | research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 Harness v4 reviewer agent implementing same 4-perspective pattern; source of design inspiration |\\n| Related item | #1430 \u2014 Confidence gating and deduplication pipeline (in-progress); consumes this item's structured verdicts |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (can be implemented independently; #1430 consolidation is optional \u2014 stub fallback covers pre-#1430 state)\\n- Blocks: #1430 \u2014 confidence gating and deduplication pipeline requires per-perspective structured verdict inputs that this item produces\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- The `agent_profile` YAML profile mechanism referenced in the target state description (`reviewer-security.yaml`) does not exist. The actual mechanism is `.md` agent files discovered by `agent_profile/discovery.py`. Implementation must use `.md` agent files \u2014 the YAML path is a fiction. Needs confirmation from item author before implementation, or treat as derivable from codebase evidence.\\n- `#1430` consolidation logic is in-progress. Until it lands, the multi-perspective-review skill must define its own minimal consolidation (collect four verdicts, apply all-APPROVE gate) rather than delegating to a not-yet-landed API.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 4 new agent definition files + 1 new skill file + 1 reference file + 1 update to complete-implementation. All follow established patterns (code-reviewer agent, forensic-review skill, TeamCreate dispatch). The verdict schema is new work but bounded in scope. Dependent on #1430 for full consolidation but can ship a working v1 with stub consolidation before that lands.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] AC6 example output contains `Performance: REJECT (1 finding)` and `Quality: APPROVE (2 minor)` \u2014 a failing run used as the format exemplar. Should use an all-APPROVE example to avoid implying a REJECT constitutes a passing gate. Gate-on-REJECT behaviour is tested by AC4; AC6 tests format only. Update the example in verdict-schema.md \u00a72.2 and the backlog item AC6 text to use all-APPROVE tokens. (reported by user review on T2)\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe development-harness plugin has language-scoped review skills: `code-review-python`, `code-review-typescript`, `code-review-cli`, `code-review-claude-skills`, `code-review-llm`, `code-review-nodejs`, `code-review-web`. Each is invoked individually based on the file type changed. There is no orchestration that dispatches multiple *perspective* reviewers in parallel against the same set of changes (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility), nor a single skill that consolidates per-perspective verdicts before the implementation is allowed to proceed.\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` (157 lines) runs `dh:code-reviewer` once per task \u2014 a single-agent, single-pass review against acceptance criteria. It does not split the review into four independent angles.\\n\\nIssue #1430 (Confidence gating and deduplication pipeline for multi-agent review findings) is complementary: it solves how to merge findings from many reviewers but does not define the *perspectives* that produce those findings. Without per-perspective scaffolding the consolidation pipeline has no inputs.\\n\\nThis is the gap Harness's `/harness-review` fills with the reviewer agent that emits one verdict per perspective (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility), each independently approving or rejecting.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe development-harness plugin has language-scoped review skills: `code-review-python`, `code-review-typescript`, `code-review-cli`, `code-review-claude-skills`, `code-review-llm`, `code-review-nodejs`, `code-review-web`. Each is invoked individually based on the file type changed. There is no orchestration that dispatches multiple *perspective* reviewers in parallel against the same set of changes (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility), nor a single skill that consolidates per-perspective verdicts before the implementation is allowed to proceed.\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` (157 lines) runs `dh:code-reviewer` once per task \u2014 a single-agent, single-pass review against acceptance criteria. It does not split the review into four independent angles.\\n\\nIssue #1430 (Confidence gating and deduplication pipeline for multi-agent review findings) is complementary: it solves how to merge findings from many reviewers but does not define the *perspectives* that produce those findings. Without per-perspective scaffolding the consolidation pipeline has no inputs.\\n\\nThis is the gap Harness's `/harness-review` fills with the reviewer agent that emits one verdict per perspective (Security, Performance, Quality, Accessibility), each independently approving or rejecting.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` that, given a diff or modified file list, dispatches four parallel `dh:task-worker` agents using `TeamCreate(\\\"review-{slug}\\\")`. Each worker is loaded with one of four perspective profiles via `profile_load`:\\n\\n- `reviewer-security` \u2014 secrets, injection, authn/authz, dependency CVE, unsafe deserialization\\n- `reviewer-performance` \u2014 N+1 queries, blocking I/O in async paths, allocations in hot loops\\n- `reviewer-quality` \u2014 naming, dead code, exception swallowing, test coverage gaps\\n- `reviewer-accessibility` \u2014 for skills producing UI/CLI/text output: ARIA equivalents, color-only signals, keyboard parity\\n\\nEach worker returns a structured verdict block: `{perspective, verdict: APPROVE|REJECT, findings: [...]}`. The skill collects all four, applies the consolidation logic from #1430 (when that lands), and gates the next pipeline stage on all-four-APPROVE (configurable threshold).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `Skill(skill=\\\"dh:multi-perspective-review\\\", args=\\\"--diff HEAD~1..HEAD\\\")` after a code change.\\n\\nExpected: four agents dispatched in parallel via `TeamCreate`, four structured verdicts collected, summary printed in format `Security: APPROVE (0 findings) | Performance: REJECT (1 finding) | Quality: APPROVE (2 minor) | Accessibility: SKIP (no UI changes)`. The skill exits non-zero when any perspective rejects.\\n\\nFiles: `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` exists; `plugins/development-harness/agent_profile/reviewer-security.yaml` and three siblings exist; `multi-perspective-review` listed in `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` quality gates.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a8f4d64eb4b43a4c69e2017d976b5c23a4571fd3ce1b623f39a6111494ae203a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCSLfg\"}"}